    "stale_discovery_behaviour": "FAIL_CLOSED",
    "stale_discovery_note": "§37 requires discovery but never says what happens when it fails or returns a truncated list. DIAL already answers this shape of question for host telemetry: stale evidence makes a target ineligible for normal work rather than silently trusted. The same rule applies here — discovery older than max_discovery_age_ms makes every model whose availability it would confirm ineligible for new routing, while work already in flight is unaffected.",
    "max_discovery_age_ms": 3600000
  },
  "qualification_note": "State records whether the model is currently present and usable on its subscription. It is not a maturity ladder and carries no notion of a model earning trust. Performance is tracked separately in MODEL_TASK_PERFORMANCE_LEDGER.json and informs ranking, never eligibility.",
  "reliability_note": "reliability_profile describes what the PROVIDER establishes about the model, not how much DIAL has used it. A model is never ranked down merely for being new to DIAL; differentiation comes from the performance ledger once real assigned jobs have produced evidence."
